detail.longDescription:
@buckfiftyseven I only use nginx on my NAS to point to different #selfhosted things on my LAN.  Like pointing `tubearchivist.lan` to my tubearchivist.  `mealie.lan` to my mealie.  Etc. Etc. Etc.

Mostly so that browsers can remember my username/password for those projects, with the added benefit that I don't have to remember what ports things are on.

Even renting a VPS with a company is an interesting security issue.  Hopefully they don't get pwned and in turn risk my VPS.
